Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||10-11-2001||09:27 AM||||my 85 gt is almost ready for the road. i got all of the parts at the salvage yard so they were pretty cheap.  here are all of the parts i bought.<P>1.left tail light $25<BR>2.shift bracket that goes on tranni $5<BR>3.coupe 1/4 windows $60<BR>4.84 shifter (i made 2" shorter) $5<BR>5.plastic shift knob (made shorter) $3<BR>6.2.8 V6 MPFI $200<P>i need a windsheild but no salvage yards have any so i will have to pay $200 for a new one and i will have to let a pro put it in.<P>the engine came out of a 86 olds cutlass ceira. after i got it home i took off the valve covers and was surprised to see that it was VERY clean under the covers. the rockers are a nice silcer color with no gunk on them at all and it looks like the heads were never taken off. <BR>all i have left to do now to get it on the road is hook up all of the vacume lines and computer wires.  <P>anyone know any sites that will tell me the hp and tq of a 86 ceira 2.8?<BR><P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <P>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw||||reg||1
